<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        A handful of addresses to look at, built in Python rather than written
        out here.

        An address is a child of a customer, and this module ships no
        customers. Pointing an XML `ref` at one would tie mart369_address to
        whichever module happened to create it. The method picks whoever is
        signed up, and does nothing at all once a 369 Mart address exists - so
        a shop with real customers never sprouts examples.

        Some of them are deliberately incomplete: a missing pincode, a missing
        mobile, no map pin. That is what the desk's tiles are for, and an
        example set where everything is perfect shows none of it.

        Not noupdate: with it the function would only run on a fresh install,
        and a shop upgrading into this feature would never see the examples.
        The method guards itself instead, so running on every upgrade is safe
        and seeds exactly once.
    -->
    <data>
        <function model="res.partner" name="_mart369_load_address_demo"/>
    </data>
</odoo>
